<JournalSupport title="Privacy" summary="How the public tools and private workspace handle your data.">
<div class="panel journal-support-card">
<h2>What stays on your device</h2><p>Public tools use memory only. The separate private workspace stores explicitly saved project data in your browser’s IndexedDB. Save inspection runs locally, and the app does not retain the raw XML.</p>
<h2>Managing your data</h2><p>Exports may include personal data you entered. Keep those files safe. You can clear stored records using your browser’s site settings. Browser extensions and anyone with access to your device may be able to read local data.</p>
<h2>Requests to this site</h2><p>The development preview has no analytics or advertising scripts. The hosting provider may process ordinary HTTP access logs.</p>
<a class="journal-return" href="/">Return to tools</a></div></JournalSupport>
